oks like marvel  studios is searching for some pretty big  guns here just like they got sam raimi  for multiverse of madness and remember  the power of marvel they did the  eternals which had an insane cast i  don't think any director is off the  table for them and according to justin  krull who is a senior reporter at  deadline marvel has a very long list of  candidates he posted to twitter last  night saying some late night fantastic  for directing search updates while it's  easily marvel's top oda one source says  don't expect it to be filled anytime  soon as they are not even close to  cutting down the long list of candidates  i'd be shocked if a choice is made  before labor day now labor day is  september 5th so that's pretty far out  there but let's continue talking about  what he said on twitter he says two  while no names have surfaced multiple  sources say while it's a large mix of  candidates feige and company are taking  a lot of shots at some big names one  source close to process says kevin  doesn't want to oversee the entire shoot  and after not having to worry about that  with sam raimi he is very game to the  same outcome with this shoot which is  kind of cool because that basically  means that kevin feige doesn't want to  oversee every single little minuscule  thing about the project but he is  putting faith in the directors that he  is hiring now this can be good but this  also can be bad depending on how you  look at it kevin feige is the founder of  the mcu he's the brains behind it  without him there wouldn't be an mcu and  kevin feige is largely responsible for  the success that it's had and part of  that is him overseeing the projects now  that's not going to change kevin feige  will always have final say with whatever  he wants from a movie when he sees it or  hears about it or reads the script so  that's why i'm not too worried about  this because kevin feige will ultimately  have final say but him letting the  directors have some freedom co